Email validator, regex check plus length caps:

```python
import re

EMAIL_RE = re.compile(
    r"^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$"
)

def is_valid_email(email: str) -> bool:
    if not email or len(email) > 254:
        return False
    local, sep, domain = email.rpartition("@")
    if not sep or len(local) > 64:
        return False
    return bool(EMAIL_RE.match(email))
```

Regex catch most format bug (no @, no domain dot, bad char). Length check per RFC 5321 (local max 64, whole max 254). Not full RFC 5322 parse — for that, use `email-validator` lib, check MX record too if need real deliverability check.
